Vanilla Minecraft 26.3 food components are derived from misode/mcmeta:
https://github.com/misode/mcmeta
Tag: 26.3-summary
Commit: d96c75fec200c4580dd75e033a76341521165461
Path: item_components/data.json
The extracted, pinned subset is food-data/foods-26.3.json.

Local changes: Android .hmod WebAssembly component, main-hand food preview,
gain-only restored hunger, original yellow saturation-gain outlines, compatible
fixed-row preview above the hunger bar with opacity-only pulse, sandbox tests,
pinned SDK, generated food/icon tables, versioned packaging, GitHub Actions and
PT-BR release reports. Current saturation is unavailable through API 0.1, so
yellow gain is right-aligned from an assumed zero baseline, not a measurement
of the player's actual saturation. This is hunger restoration, not estimated
health regeneration.
